{
  "explanation": "The attacker attempted a brute-force or credential stuffing attack by sending multiple HTTP POST requests to the `/api/login` endpoint using various source IPs within the same subnet. The resulting HTTP 401 Unauthorized status codes indicate that the authentication attempts failed, but the high frequency of requests shows automated malicious activity targeting user credentials.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement rate limiting and account lockout policies on the `/api/login` endpoint to mitigate automated brute-force attacks.",
    "Block or challenge suspicious traffic originating from the malicious IP subnet (185.199.10.0/24) at the web application firewall (WAF) or edge proxy layer.",
    "Enforce Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) across all user accounts to protect against compromised credentials."
  ]
}
